From c798ea6ef5a563c7a1bb2f973cda14d1dac91940 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wine-thumbs <wine-thumbs@localhost>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 16:19:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] shell32: Add a thumbnail view mode.

FVM_THUMBNAIL was accepted but drawn like the list view. Image files are
now decoded with WIC on a small pool of background threads, downscaled
with an area-averaging filter (the WIC scaler only does nearest
neighbour), oriented according to EXIF and kept in a process-wide cache.
Other items show their shell icon rendered from the 256px image list.

The list view keeps doing layout, labels and selection; items are drawn
through custom draw so thumbnails are not tinted by the selection blend.
The size can be changed with HKCU\Software\Wine\Thumbnails "Size" (in
96 DPI pixels, default 96) and the cache with "CacheSize" (MB, default 64).
